    "Description": "THOMAS STONE NATIONAL HISTORIC SITE - INSTALL INTERIOR STORM WINDOWS The National Park Service, Contracting Operations East, New England Major Acquisition Buying Office, issues this contract for a construction requirement at Thomas Stone National Historic Site in Port Tobacco, Maryland. Work consists of furnishing all labor, supervision, materials, tools, supplies, transportation, license, certificates, permits, personal protection equipment, professional services, and equipment as required to provide and install magnetic interior storm windows as detailed in the Scope of Work, included with the award documents. Attachment 1 - Scope of Work - 04/02/2026 Attachment 2 - DOL Construction Wage Rate Determination - 05/18/2026 Attachment 3 - Construction Contract Administration - 05/20/2026",
